2. THE FRONT END'S REGULATION (VOUT = VREF x (1 + R6 / R7); VREF 0.788 / 0.800 / 0.812 V, SNVSAI1D 6.5 p.6)
   nominal                                         20.000 V
   VREF and the printed 1 % only                   19.326 to 20.694 V
   with 100 ppm/K over 65 K (INFERRED) and IBIAS(FB) 25 nA both ways (p.6, 6.1 mV)   19.080 to 20.960 V   <- the DC band

3. THE FRONT END'S OUTPUT OVER-VOLTAGE PROTECTION (SNVSAI1D 6.5 p.8; 7.3.11 p.18; 7.1 p.13)
   threshold at FB: VREF + 10 % TYPICAL (no minimum or maximum given), hysteresis 2.5 %; response: 'turns off the gate
   drives' (7.3.11) or 'the high-side drivers' (7.1); either stops the input's energy (Q2 off blocks VIN_RAW). OVP reads FB,
   so it scales with the same divider: the bus trips at 1.10 x its own regulation.
   trip, nominal                                   22.000 V
   trip, VREF maximum and the divider's worst ratio 23.055 V   (INFERRED: TI's 10 % is typical only)
   L1's energy after the trip: the boost peak limit 140 mV / (5 mOhm - 1 %) = 28.28 A (p.7), L1 +20 % = 12 uH:
   4.80 mJ into the six bulk parts at -20 % (1.584 mF, ceramics not counted) lifts the bus to 23.186 V   <- the bound
   (L1 saturates at 17.5 A, so 0.5 L I^2 at 28 A overstates the energy: the bound is high by it)
   the typical 10 % would have to be wrong by this much before the bus reaches each limit (VREF max, worst ratio, residue):
      24.0 V (80 % of the FETs' 30 V): an OVP 13.9 % over VREF
      26.0 V (the BQ25731's recommended 26 V and ACOV's minimum): an OVP 23.4 % over VREF
      30.0 V (the FETs' 30 V): an OVP 42.5 % over VREF
      32.0 V (the BQ25731's absolute 32 V): an OVP 52.1 % over VREF

4. A LOAD DUMP: THE CHARGER STOPS AT ITS FULL INPUT CURRENT
   The charger's own inductor L2 does not feed VBUS20 when it stops: with Q7 off its current returns through Q8 to VBAT
   (Q10's body diode points to VBAT). The front end sees a load step and answers with its loop (MODEL: crossover
   0.71 kHz at its slowest corner, |Zout| 89 mOhm, gen_sch_a.py lines 722 to 724); its CCM stage can sink current
   (SNVSAI1D 7.3.8). Step dI into the bulk at -20 %: dV = dI / (2 pi fc C), plus L1's stored energy:
   6.45 A (Option A(i)'s bound, U3's 6.35 A clamp plus 0.1 A): loop 0.913 V, |Zout| 0.574 V; with L1's 1.57 mJ (16.2 A, gen_sch_a.py line 751) the peak is 21.918 V
   8.00 A (VBUS20's declared peak): loop 1.132 V, |Zout| 0.712 V; with L1's 1.57 mJ (16.2 A, gen_sch_a.py line 751) the peak is 22.137 V
   (MODEL; below the OVP trip's 23.055 V, so OVP need not act; whatever the model's error, section 3 caps it at 23.186 V)
   During the dump the charger is not switching: Q7 and Q8 then block the bus alone, VDS at most the bus plus Q8's
   body diode (SLPS516 VSD 1.0 V maximum): 23.14 V.

5. THE FRONT END'S INPUT (what board E delivers into VIN_RAW)
   service 9 to 36 V (REQ-015); board E's LM5069 opens its pass FET at OVLO 37.78 / 40.09 / 42.49 V (OVLOTH 2.4 / 2.5 / 2.6 V,
   SNVS452G 6.5 p.5, over R22 100k and R23 6.65k at 1 %); the panel tracker's TRK_OUT (15.1 V) joins through an ideal
   diode; four SMCJ40A class clamps (board E D10 SMCJ40CA, D1 and D2, board A D2): VBR 44.4 to 49.1 V, VC 64.5 V at 23.3 A
   (Littelfuse, page 2 of 6). U2 regulates VBUS20 for any VIN from 4.2 to 55 V (SNVSAI1D 6.3 p.5); a line step reaches
   the bus only through the loop. MODEL, valley current mode at L1 -20 %, fSW 175 kHz: the ripple rises from
   6.25 A at 36 V to 9.74 A at U2's 60 V, the average by 1.74 A until the loop answers: 0.247 V on the bus (21.207 V).
   With U2 idle Q2 blocks VIN_RAW (section 1). Above 55 V U2 leaves its recommended range and above 60 V its absolute
   ratings (VIN, VISNS, VOSNS 60 V, p.5): the clamps' 64.5 V is S-111's item; this bound assumes U2 inside its ratings.

6. CLAMPS
   on VBUS20: none (section 1). Upstream: the four SMCJ40A class parts of section 5. On VBAT: D1 SMCJ18A (VR 18 V,
   VBR 20.00 to 22.10 V, VC 29.2 V at 51.4 A).

7. THE PACK SIDE (Q10's drain and, in buck mode, Q9's drain through Q10)
   ChargeVoltage 16.8 V + 0.5 % = 16.884 V (SLUSE66A 8.5 p.9); BATOVP at most 105 % = 17.64 V (p.14); SYSOVP (4S) 19.0 / 19.5 /
   20.0 V turns the converter off (p.14). A pack that opens while charging at A2's 15.71 A: SYSOVP stops the converter at
   20.0 V and L2's 0.70 mJ goes into VBAT's own capacitance (its effective value under bias is not held: INCONCLUSIVE);
   D1 bounds it: 24.27 V at 15.71 A (INFERRED, the straight line from VBR max at 1 mA to VC at IPP), 29.2 V at its IPP.

