10. THE SWITCH NODES: A BUDGET, NOT A BOUND (INCONCLUSIVE at desk)
   No layout exists (S-115) and no TI application note giving a layout-independent ringing bound is held. What TI does
   state: '30 V or higher voltage rating MOSFETs are preferred for 19-V to 20-V input voltage' (SLUSE66A 10.2.2.6 p.86),
   in a topology whose hot loop runs through RAC with at most 10 nF + 1 nF after it (p.86; Figure 10-1 p.83), as board A
   draws it. Board A's DC band tops out 0.96 V above TI's 20 V.
   Budget left for ringing over the steady bus (20.96 V) and over the bound (23.19 V):
     Q7 VDS (the bus plus SW1's undershoot) and Q8 VDS (SW1's overshoot), 30 V       9.04 /  6.81 V
     U3 SW1 absolute 32 V                                                           11.04 /  8.81 V
     U3 SW1 recommended 26 V                                                         5.04 /  2.81 V
     U3 SW1 below ground: -2 V, and -4 V for 25 ns (p.8)
   MODEL for the layout writer (not a bound): Q7's current falls in (Qgs - Qg(th)) / (VPLT / (RDS_HI_OFF + RG)) =
   1.4 nC / (2.7 V / (1.3 + 1.8 Ohm)) = 1.61 ns (SLPS526 p.3; SLUSE66A p.16, typical; plateau INFERRED); each nH of
   hot loop then adds L x di/dt, and each nH between the VBUS20 bank and C190 / C191 lifts CH_ACN by I x sqrt(L / 11 nF):
     A2, L2 peak 15.71 A:  9.77 A/ns, 9.77 V per nH of loop and 4.74 V per nH before C190; for the 30 V budget 0.92 nH, for 26 V 0.52 nH
     G1, L2 peak 14.10 A:  8.77 A/ns, 8.77 V per nH of loop and 4.25 V per nH before C190; for the 30 V budget 1.03 nH, for 26 V 0.57 nH
     A1, L2 peak 10.70 A:  6.66 A/ns, 6.66 V per nH of loop and 3.23 V per nH before C190; for the 30 V budget 1.36 nH, for 26 V 0.76 nH
   Avalanche, if a ring does pass 30 V: EAS 23 mJ (CSD17578Q5A) and 39 mJ (CSD17577Q5A), single pulse, p.1; a repetitive
   rating is not stated, so no margin is taken from it.

11. SINGLE FAULTS OUTSIDE EVERY REQUIREMENT (ASM-001 refuses 'no single point of failure'; SC-39)
   Q2 shorted: VBUS20 = VIN_RAW less Q5's body diode (about 0.8 V, INFERRED), 35.2 V at 36 V in and 41.7 V at board E's
   OVLO maximum; U3's ACOV (26.0 to 27.7 V, 100 us) stops the charger, and above 32.8 V in U3's VBUS, ACP and ACN pass
   their 32 V absolute rating. With the charger stopped Q7 and Q8 are both off and share the bus through their leakage
   and L2 to VBAT (INFERRED), so U3 is the first part past its rating, not the FETs.
   R6 open or FB shorted: OVP reads the same pin, so nothing on board A bounds the bus; the 35 V bulk parts and U3's
   32 V are passed. Neither fault is bounded by the FETs' rating: 40 V parts would not keep U3 inside 32 V.
   Not taken, for the qualified power review (S-111): an independent over-voltage trip on VBUS20 (a second divider into
   U34's channel 1, re-armed while the stage runs) would bound the FB faults; an SMCJ22A on VBUS20 (VR 22 V over the
   20.96 V DC band) would hold a Q2 short at about 28.2 V at board E's 6.15 A hot-swap limit (INFERRED straight line)
   until the LM5069's fault timer opens, and clamps 35.5 V at its own IPP, over 30 V.

12. THE ANSWER: (a), the bound holds in service
   VBUS20 stays at or under 23.19 V by the front end's own protection whatever the load, the line or the loop model does,
   6.81 V under the FETs' 30 V and 8.81 V under U3's 32 V; U3's ACOV (26.0 V minimum) is never reached. The pack side stays
   at or under 20.0 V by SYSOVP and 24.27 V by D1 in a pack that opens while charging. The switch nodes are INCONCLUSIVE:
   ringing is a layout and bench item with 9.04 V of budget over the steady bus, carried as its own open item.
